infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Three fixes for the lost update — pick by contention profile
  desc All three close the stale-read-then-write gap; they differ in how a hot wallet behaves
  lists
    - label Pessimistic lock — SELECT … FOR UPDATE
      desc Lock the wallet row before reading, so the second debit blocks and reads the fresh balance. Simple and exactly correct, but a hot wallet serializes into a queue.
    - label Optimistic / CAS — version check
      desc Read balance + version, write only if the version is unchanged (WHERE id=? AND version=?); on conflict, zero rows hit and you retry. Great when contention is rare, storms with retries when it is high.
    - label Atomic conditional write — single statement
      desc Push check-and-decrement into one operation: UPDATE … SET balance = balance - 70 WHERE balance >= 70. No read-modify-write race exists; zero rows means insufficient funds. The cleanest single-wallet debit.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
